/-!
# Ascent of the Serre property `(R_k)` along a flat ring map

All rings are commutative with unit. A Noetherian local ring `(A, 𝔪)` with residue field
`k = A/𝔪` is *regular* if the minimal number of generators of its maximal ideal equals its
Krull dimension, equivalently `dim_k (𝔪/𝔪²) = dim A`; in Mathlib this is
`IsRegularLocalRing`.

For a Noetherian ring `A` and an integer `k ≥ 0`, `A` has *property `(R_k)`* if for every prime
`p` of `A` with `ht p ≤ k` the local ring `A_p` is regular. Since `dim (A_p) = ht p`, the height
condition is the same as `dim (A_p) ≤ k`.

For a ring map `φ : R → S` and a prime `p` of `R`, the *fibre ring* of `φ` over `p` is
`S ⊗[R] κ(p)`, where `κ(p) = Frac(R/p)` is the residue field of `R` at `p`; in Mathlib `κ(p)`
is `IsLocalRing.ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p)`.

## Main result

`property_Rk_of_flat_of_fibre_of_base`: let `φ : R → S` be a flat ring map with `R` and `S`
Noetherian and fix `k ≥ 0`. If every fibre ring `S ⊗[R] κ(p)` has `(R_k)` and `R` has `(R_k)`,
then `S` has `(R_k)`.

The two non-trivial inputs are the dimension formula for flat local homomorphisms, available as
`Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown`, and the ascent of regularity along a
flat local map with regular closed fibre. Flatness of `φ` supplies `Algebra.HasGoingDown R S`
via `HasGoingDown.of_flat`, the hypothesis needed by the dimension formula.

At a fixed prime `q ⊂ S` of height `≤ k` lying over `p = φ⁻¹(q)`, the argument reduces to two
further inputs, neither present in Mathlib as a named declaration:

* the localization of the fibre ring `S ⊗[R] κ(p)` at the prime corresponding to `q` is
  isomorphic to the closed fibre `S_q / p S_q`, which together with the height equality lets
  the fibre hypothesis deliver regularity of `S_q / p S_q`;
* regularity ascends along a flat local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings with regular
  base and regular closed fibre (`isRegularLocalRing_of_flat_of_regular_closedFibre`).

Both are stated as named sub-lemmas below; the dimension-formula step is discharged inside the
main proof.
-/

@[expose] public section

/-! ### Regularity ascent along a flat local homomorphism

Let `A → B` be a flat local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings: `A` and `B` are local via
`IsLocalRing`, the map is `algebraMap A B` and is local via `IsLocalHom`, and `B` is flat over
`A`. If `A` is a regular local ring and the closed fibre `B / 𝔪_A B` is a regular local ring,
then `B` is a regular local ring.

Write `𝔪 = 𝔪_A` and `𝔫 = 𝔪_B`. Because `A → B` is flat and local, the dimension formula gives
`dim B = dim A + dim (B/𝔪B)`. A regular system of parameters of `A` maps to a regular sequence
in `B`, flatness preserving regular sequences over the base, and a regular system of parameters
of the closed fibre `B/𝔪B` lifts to elements of `𝔫`; their union is a system of
`dim A + dim (B/𝔪B) = dim B` elements generating `𝔫`, since the images generate `𝔫/𝔪B` and
`𝔪B` is generated by the images of the regular system of parameters of `A`. Hence `𝔫` is
generated by `dim B` elements, so `B` is regular. Equivalently, via embedding dimension,
`embdim B = embdim A + embdim (B/𝔪B)` for flat local maps and `embdim = dim` on each regular
factor, giving `embdim B = dim A + dim (B/𝔪B) = dim B`.
-/

/-- Generation subadditivity for `spanFinrank` along a quotient: if `I ≤ p` are
ideals of a Noetherian ring, then a minimal generating set of `p` is no larger
than (a minimal generating set of `I`) together with (lifts of a minimal
generating set of the image `p / I = Ideal.map (Quotient.mk I) p`). This is the
"a regular system of parameters of the base maps to part of one upstairs, and a
regular system of parameters of the closed fibre lifts to the rest" content of
the Stacks 031E argument, isolated as an elementary ring-theoretic fact. -/
theorem spanFinrank_le_add_spanFinrank_map_quotient
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] {I p : Ideal R} (h : I ≤ p) :
    p.spanFinrank ≤ I.spanFinrank + (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) p).spanFinrank := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨sI, hsI_card, hsI_span⟩ :=
    (IsNoetherian.noetherian I).exists_span_finset_card_eq_spanFinrank
  obtain ⟨t, ht_card, ht_span⟩ :=
    (IsNoetherian.noetherian (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
        p)).exists_span_finset_card_eq_spanFinrank
  set f := Ideal.Quotient.mk I
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective f := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hlift : ∀ y ∈ t, ∃ a, a ∈ p ∧ f a = y := by
    intro y hy
    have hymem : y ∈ Ideal.map f p := by rw [← ht_span]; exact Submodule.subset_span hy
    exact (Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective f hsurj).mp hymem
  choose g hg using hlift
  set lifts : Finset R := t.attach.image (fun y => g y.val y.property) with hlifts
  set T : Finset R := sI ∪ lifts with hT
  have hsub : (t : Set (R ⧸ I)) ⊆ f '' (lifts : Set R) := by
    intro y hy
    refine ⟨g y hy, ?_, (hg y hy).right⟩
    simp only [hlifts, Finset.coe_image]
    exact ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, Finset.mem_attach _ _, rfl⟩
  have hpre : ∀ z ∈ Submodule.span (R ⧸ I) (f '' (lifts : Set R)),
      ∃ n ∈ Submodule.span R (lifts : Set R), f n = z := by
    intro z hz
    induction hz using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
        obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hx
        exact ⟨a, Submodule.subset_span ha, rfl⟩
    | zero => exact ⟨0, Submodule.zero_mem _, by simp⟩
    | add x y hx hy ihx ihy =>
        obtain ⟨nx, hnx, hnxe⟩ := ihx
        obtain ⟨ny, hny, hnye⟩ := ihy
        exact ⟨nx + ny, Submodule.add_mem _ hnx hny, by rw [map_add, hnxe, hnye]⟩
    | smul c x hx ih =>
        obtain ⟨n, hn, hne⟩ := ih
        obtain ⟨c', rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective c
        exact ⟨c' * n, Submodule.smul_mem _ c' hn, by rw [map_mul, hne]; rfl⟩
  have hspan : Submodule.span R (T : Set R) = p := by
    apply le_antisymm
    · rw [Submodule.span_le]
      intro x hx
      simp only [hT, Finset.coe_union, Set.mem_union] at hx
      rcases hx with hx | hx
      · have : x ∈ I := by rw [← hsI_span]; exact Submodule.subset_span hx
        exact h this
      · simp only [hlifts, Finset.coe_image, Set.mem_image, Finset.mem_coe] at hx
        obtain ⟨y, _, rfl⟩ := hx
        exact (hg y.val y.property).left
    · intro x hx
      have hfx : f x ∈ Ideal.map f p := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem f hx
      rw [← ht_span] at hfx
      have hfx2 : f x ∈ Submodule.span (R ⧸ I) (f '' (lifts : Set R)) :=
        Submodule.span_mono hsub hfx
      obtain ⟨n, hn_mem, hn_eq⟩ := hpre _ hfx2
      have hnT : n ∈ Submodule.span R (T : Set R) := by
        apply Submodule.span_mono _ hn_mem
        simp only [hT, Finset.coe_union]; exact Set.subset_union_right
      have hxn : x - n ∈ I := (Ideal.Quotient.eq).mp hn_eq.symm
      have hxnT : x - n ∈ Submodule.span R (T : Set R) := by
        rw [← hsI_span] at hxn
        apply Submodule.span_mono _ hxn
        simp only [hT, Finset.coe_union]; exact Set.subset_union_left
      rw [← sub_add_cancel x n]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ hxnT hnT
  calc p.spanFinrank = (Submodule.span R (T : Set R)).spanFinrank := by rw [hspan]
    _ ≤ (T : Set R).ncard := Submodule.spanFinrank_span_le_ncard_of_finite (Set.toFinite _)
    _ ≤ T.card := (Set.ncard_coe_finset T).le
    _ ≤ sI.card + lifts.card := Finset.card_union_le _ _
    _ ≤ sI.card + t.card := by
        gcongr
        exact Finset.card_image_le.trans_eq t.card_attach
    _ = I.spanFinrank + (Ideal.map f p).spanFinrank := by rw [hsI_card, ht_card]

/-- Regularity ascends along a flat local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings with regular
base and regular closed fibre: if `A → B` is flat and local, `A` is a regular local ring and
`B / 𝔪_A B` is a regular local ring, then `B` is a regular local ring. -/
@[ega "0 17.3.3",
  ega "IV 17.5.8" "(iii)",
  ega "IV 6.5.1",
  ega "IV 6.5.2" "(ii), special case",
  ega "IV 7.5.1.1" "special case",
  ega "IV 7.5.3" "more general",
  ega "IV 7.5.4" "(iii), special case", sga "1 I 9.1" "ascent", sga "6 X 7.7" "special case"]
theorem isRegularLocalRing_of_flat_of_regular_closedFibre
    (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsLocalRing B] [Module.Flat A B]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
    (hA : IsRegularLocalRing A)
    (hfib : IsRegularLocalRing
      (B ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap A B) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))) :
    IsRegularLocalRing B := by
  -- Let `I = 𝔪_A · B = Ideal.map (algebraMap A B) 𝔪_A`; then `B ⧸ I` is the closed
  -- fibre `F`, regular by `hfib`, hence local.
  set I : Ideal B := Ideal.map (algebraMap A B) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) with hI
  have hFloc : IsLocalRing (B ⧸ I) := hfib.toIsLocalRing
  have : Algebra.HasGoingDown A B := Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat
  have hlo : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :=
    IsLocalRing.ResidueField.instLiesOverMaximalIdeal
  -- `I ≤ 𝔫_B` since the map is local (`𝔪_A` lies under `𝔫_B`).
  have hIle : I ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B := by
    rw [hI, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro a ha
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap]
    have h := hlo.over
    rw [h, Ideal.mem_comap] at ha; exact ha
  -- The maximal ideal of `F = B ⧸ I` is the image of `𝔫_B`.
  have hmaxF : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (B ⧸ I)
      = Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) :=
    (IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective).symm
  -- S1 (tag 00ON), in local form: the flat-local dimension formula, as heights.
  --   ht(𝔫_B) = ht(𝔪_A) + ht(image of 𝔫_B in F).
  have hform := Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
  -- Generation subadditivity: spanFinrank 𝔫_B ≤ spanFinrank I + spanFinrank 𝔫_F.
  have hsub : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).spanFinrank ≤
      I.spanFinrank
        + (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)).spanFinrank :=
    spanFinrank_le_add_spanFinrank_map_quotient hIle
  -- spanFinrank(I) ≤ spanFinrank(𝔪_A), since `I` is the image of `𝔪_A`.
  have hIspan : I.spanFinrank ≤ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).spanFinrank := by
    rw [hI]
    exact Ideal.spanFinrank_map_le_of_fg (algebraMap A B) (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)
  -- It suffices to show `spanFinrank 𝔫_B ≤ dim B`.
  apply IsRegularLocalRing.of_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le
  -- Regularity rewrites embedding dimension as Krull dimension on `A` and `F`.
  have hAeq : (↑(Submodule.spanFinrank (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)) : WithBot ℕ∞)
      = ringKrullDim A := hA.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal
  have hFeq : (↑(Submodule.spanFinrank
        (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B))) : WithBot ℕ∞)
      = ringKrullDim (B ⧸ I) := by
    rw [← hmaxF]; exact hfib.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal
  -- `ht = dim` for the maximal ideals of the local rings `A`, `B`, `F`.
  have hAh : (↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).height : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim A :=
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim
  have hBh : (↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).height : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim B :=
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim
  have hFh : (↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (B ⧸ I)).height : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim (B ⧸ I) :=
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim
  have key : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).spanFinrank ≤
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).spanFinrank
        + (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)).spanFinrank := by
    calc (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).spanFinrank ≤ I.spanFinrank + _ := hsub
      _ ≤ _ := by gcongr
  -- Assemble: embdim B ≤ embdim A + embdim F = dim A + dim F = dim B.
  calc (↑(Submodule.spanFinrank (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)) : WithBot ℕ∞)
      ≤ ↑((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).spanFinrank
          + (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)).spanFinrank) := by
        exact_mod_cast key
    _ = (↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).spanFinrank : WithBot ℕ∞)
          + ↑(Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)).spanFinrank := by
        push_cast; ring
    _ = ringKrullDim A + ringKrullDim (B ⧸ I) := by rw [hAeq, hFeq]
    _ = (↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).height : WithBot ℕ∞)
          + ↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (B ⧸ I)).height := by rw [hAh, hFh]
    _ = (↑((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).height
          + (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal
              B)).height) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
        rw [hmaxF]; push_cast; ring
    _ = (↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).height : WithBot ℕ∞) := by rw [← hform]
    _ = ringKrullDim B := hBh

